PREFIX = """VISUAL LANGUAGE — Photorealistic live-action woodland mystery, intimate and restrained, never fantasy spectacle. Natural skin texture, damp fabric, real breath and weight, subtle film grain, gentle halation, softly lifted blacks, fine highlight rolloff; no CGI sheen, no game-engine look.
CINEMATOGRAPHY — 2.39:1 anamorphic composition, physical vintage spherical lenses with mild edge softness, shallow depth of field used selectively, deliberate locked frames or slow human-operated movement only. Keep the 180-degree shutter feel and natural motion blur.
LIGHT — Overcast late-morning daylight filtered through a dense deciduous canopy; soft cool top light, faint mist between distant trunks, no visible sun shafts and no artificial light.
COLOR — Forest greens and wet charcoal dominate, muted skin and weathered olive secondary, graphite-silver accent. Low saturation, cool-neutral grade, white balance near 5000K.
CONTINUITY — The man is early 30s, lean, tousled dark-brown hair, short stubble, tired brown eyes, faded charcoal henley under a weathered olive field jacket, mud-darkened black jeans and worn brown leather boots. His face, hair, clothing, mud marks and proportions remain identical in all clips. He begins with damp leaves stuck to his right shoulder and jacket back. The forest is the same continuous place: beech and oak trunks, fern understory, wet leaf litter, thin ground mist. The child must never appear before explicitly introduced.
PERFORMANCE — Underplayed natural acting through breath, eye-lines, hesitation and small involuntary movements; never theatrical fear, mugging or exaggerated panic.
PHYSICS — Real gravity, footfall weight, foliage contact, cloth movement and contact shadows. Leaves compress under bodies and boots. Mist never moves like smoke.
TECHNICAL — 24fps, real-time motion, stable identity and anatomy, consistent screen direction. No slow motion, speed ramps, frame interpolation artifacts, morphing, flicker or temporal jumps.
AUDIO — Diegetic forest ambience, clothing, footsteps, breathing, pencil and spoken dialogue only. No music, narration, subtitles or added cinematic booms."""


